  "doctrine": {
    "summary": "Oil-funded army trained to Turkish standards that won the 2020 war and took Nagorno-Karabakh in 2023 through drones (Bayraktar TB2, Harop and other Israeli loitering munitions), precision artillery and special forces infiltration in mountains. Equipment mixes Russian armour (T-90S, T-72, BMP-3, BTR-82A), Israeli and Turkish systems and Serbian guns. Relations with Russia were badly damaged in 2025 (AZAL airliner, Yekaterinburg deaths) and are now a 'cold' formal normalisation.",
    "squad_size": 9,
    "fireteam": "Turkish-style 9-man squad (two fireteams); special forces in small teams. Game: 8 in pairs.",
    "tactics": [
      "Drone-first: ISR and loitering munitions hit armour, artillery and air defence before ground moves",
      "Special forces infiltrate mountain ridgelines at night",
      "Precision artillery and MLRS on located targets",
      "Mechanised follow-up with T-90/T-72 and BMP-3"
    ],
